# SS13 Framework asset credits
#
# Every file under a project's src/<set>/resources/assets/ directory, or under
# the assets/ of a built-in resource pack in src/<set>/resources/resourcepacks/,
# has one entry here. All assets are licensed CC BY-SA 4.0 International;
# see LICENSE-ASSETS. scripts/check_credits.py checks this file in CI.
#
# Format
#
# An entry is a block of "key: value" lines. Blank lines separate entries.
# Lines starting with "#" are comments. Each entry starts with "path", the
# file's path from the repository root, with forward slashes, followed by
# "origin": original, vgstation13 or other.
#
# An asset drawn from scratch for the framework:
#
#   path: ss13-framework/src/main/resources/assets/ss13_framework/textures/item/machine_frame.png
#   origin: original
#
# An asset derived from a vgstation13 sprite:
#
#   path: ss13-framework/src/main/resources/assets/ss13_framework/textures/item/circuit_board.png
#   origin: vgstation13
#   source: icons/obj/module.dmi
#   state: circuit_board
#   commit: 0123456789ab
#
#   source       the .dmi file, as a path in the vgstation13 repository.
#                List several separated by ", " when an asset draws on more
#                than one. Never a file under goon/ (CC BY-NC-SA).
#   state        the icon state used. List several separated by ", ".
#   commit       the vgstation13 commit hash, 7 to 40 hex digits.
#   attribution  optional; defaults to "vgstation13 contributors, CC BY-SA 3.0 US".
#
# A sound taken from vgstation13. Its source is the file under vg's sound/, and
# it has no state. "adapted" says how the file was changed, if it was:
#
#   path: ss13-framework/src/main/resources/assets/ss13_framework/sounds/tool/hum.ogg
#   origin: vgstation13
#   source: sound/ambience/ambiatm1.ogg
#   commit: 0123456789ab
#   adapted: Mixed to mono, cut to a loop and levelled.
#
# An asset taken or adapted from any other source:
#
#   path: ss13-framework/src/main/resources/assets/ss13_framework/sounds/hiss.ogg
#   origin: other
#   source: https://example.org/sounds/hiss
#   license: CC-BY-4.0
#   attribution: Jane Doe
#
#   source       where it came from: a URL, or a description if there is none.
#   license      its SPDX license id. Allowed, because they can be adapted
#                under CC BY-SA 4.0: CC0-1.0, CC-BY-3.0, CC-BY-4.0,
#                CC-BY-SA-3.0, CC-BY-SA-4.0. NonCommercial (NC) and
#                NoDerivatives (ND) licenses are never allowed.
#                A file under font/ may instead keep Bitstream-Vera.
#   attribution  the author to credit, as the license asks. Required except
#                for CC0-1.0.
#
# Any entry may add "author: <name>" (who made or adapted the file for the framework)
# and "notes: <text>". If an asset's origin or license is unclear, leave it
# out.
#
# Run the check locally with: python scripts/check_credits.py

